# 26 U.S.C. § 32 — Earned income

An independent encoding of the federal Earned Income Tax Credit,
written directly from the statute text (and the inflation-adjusted
amounts of Rev. Proc. 2022-38 for tax year 2023), deliberately without
consulting PolicyEngine's implementation. Lawlib transpiles this into
Lean and compares it, definition by definition, against the
PolicyEngine-derived encoding: agreement becomes an equivalence
theorem; disagreement becomes a finding.

Scope note: this encodes the credit *computation* of §32(a)–(b) — the
amounts and percentages — for an eligible individual. Eligibility
(§32(c)(1), §32(i) investment income, identification requirements) is
the caller's burden here, mirroring the comparison boundary used for
the Lean theorems.

```catala-metadata
declaration scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  input earned_income content money
  input adjusted_gross_income content money
  input qualifying_children content integer
  input joint_return content boolean
  internal credit_percentage content decimal
  internal phaseout_percentage content decimal
  internal earned_income_amount content money
  internal phaseout_amount content money
  internal credit_before_limitation content money
  internal income_over_phaseout content money
  internal limitation content money
  output credit content money
```

## § 32(a)(1) — In general

  In the case of an eligible individual, there shall be allowed as a
  credit against the tax imposed by this subtitle for the taxable year
  an amount equal to the credit percentage of so much of the
  taxpayer's earned income for the taxable year as does not exceed the
  earned income amount.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  definition credit_before_limitation equals
    credit_percentage
      * (if earned_income >= earned_income_amount
         then earned_income_amount
         else earned_income)
```

## § 32(a)(2) — Limitation

  The amount of the credit allowable to a taxpayer under paragraph (1)
  for any taxable year shall not exceed the excess (if any) of —
  (A) the credit percentage of the earned income amount, over
  (B) the phaseout percentage of so much of the adjusted gross income
  (or, if greater, the earned income) of the taxpayer for the taxable
  year as exceeds the phaseout amount.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  definition income_over_phaseout equals
    if adjusted_gross_income >= earned_income then
      (if adjusted_gross_income >= phaseout_amount
       then adjusted_gross_income - phaseout_amount
       else $0)
    else
      (if earned_income >= phaseout_amount
       then earned_income - phaseout_amount
       else $0)

  definition limitation equals
    if credit_percentage * earned_income_amount
         >= phaseout_percentage * income_over_phaseout
    then credit_percentage * earned_income_amount
           - phaseout_percentage * income_over_phaseout
    else $0

  definition credit equals
    if credit_before_limitation >= limitation
    then limitation
    else credit_before_limitation
```

## § 32(b)(1) — Percentages

  In the case of an eligible individual with: 1 qualifying child, the
  credit percentage is 34 and the phaseout percentage is 15.98; 2
  qualifying children, 40 and 21.06; 3 or more qualifying children, 45
  and 21.06; no qualifying children, 7.65 and 7.65.

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  definition credit_percentage equals
    if qualifying_children = 0 then 7.65%
    else if qualifying_children = 1 then 34%
    else if qualifying_children = 2 then 40%
    else 45%

  definition phaseout_percentage equals
    if qualifying_children = 0 then 7.65%
    else if qualifying_children = 1 then 15.98%
    else 21.06%
```

## § 32(b)(2) — Amounts, as adjusted by § 32(j) for 2023

The earned income amount and the phaseout amount, with the § 32(j)
inflation adjustments for taxable year 2023 (Rev. Proc. 2022-38,
§ 2.06; phaseout amounts include the § 32(b)(2)(B) increase for joint
returns, as adjusted):

```catala
scope EarnedIncomeCredit:
  definition earned_income_amount equals
    if qualifying_children = 0 then $7,840
    else if qualifying_children = 1 then $11,750
    else $16,510

  definition phaseout_amount equals
    if joint_return then
      (if qualifying_children = 0 then $16,370 else $28,120)
    else
      (if qualifying_children = 0 then $9,800 else $21,560)
```

## Test scopes

Interpreted with `catala interpret --no-stdlib -s <scope>`.

```catala
declaration scope TestPlateau1Child:
  output result content EarnedIncomeCredit

scope TestPlateau1Child:
  definition result equals
    output of EarnedIncomeCredit with
      { -- earned_income: $20,000
        -- adjusted_gross_income: $20,000
        -- qualifying_children: 1
        -- joint_return: false }

declaration scope TestPhaseIn1Child:
  output result content EarnedIncomeCredit

scope TestPhaseIn1Child:
  definition result equals
    output of EarnedIncomeCredit with
      { -- earned_income: $10,000
        -- adjusted_gross_income: $10,000
        -- qualifying_children: 1
        -- joint_return: false }

declaration scope TestPhaseOut1Child:
  output result content EarnedIncomeCredit

scope TestPhaseOut1Child:
  definition result equals
    output of EarnedIncomeCredit with
      { -- earned_income: $30,000
        -- adjusted_gross_income: $30,000
        -- qualifying_children: 1
        -- joint_return: false }

declaration scope TestChildlessPlateau:
  output result content EarnedIncomeCredit

scope TestChildlessPlateau:
  definition result equals
    output of EarnedIncomeCredit with
      { -- earned_income: $7,900
        -- adjusted_gross_income: $7,900
        -- qualifying_children: 0
        -- joint_return: false }

declaration scope TestThreeKidsJointPlateau:
  output result content EarnedIncomeCredit

scope TestThreeKidsJointPlateau:
  definition result equals
    output of EarnedIncomeCredit with
      { -- earned_income: $20,000
        -- adjusted_gross_income: $20,000
        -- qualifying_children: 3
        -- joint_return: true }

declaration scope TestChildlessZeroPoint:
  output result content EarnedIncomeCredit

scope TestChildlessZeroPoint:
  definition result equals
    output of EarnedIncomeCredit with
      { -- earned_income: $17,640
        -- adjusted_gross_income: $17,640
        -- qualifying_children: 0
        -- joint_return: false }
```
